  WE MODIFY IT. One line of srtcore/core.cpp is changed at build time, and
  the change is reproduced in full in that same CMakeLists.txt as the
  PATCH_COMMAND of the libsrt ExternalProject, which is the Modified
  Source Code this notice is obliged to point at. In the check that
  libsrt 1.5.7 added at the top of CUDT::processCtrl,

      if (!pktlen || pktlen % sizeof(int32_t) != 0)

  becomes

      if (pktlen % sizeof(int32_t) != 0)

  so that a control packet with no payload is accepted, as it was in
  1.5.6 and earlier. An ACKACK has no Control Information Field by
  specification (draft-sharabayko-srt-01 section 3.2.8), and senders that
  send it that way were otherwise losing the receiver's RTT estimate, its
  NAK pacing and its clock-drift correction. Build with
  -PacceptEmptyAckAck=false for stock libsrt.

